`--across-face SYSTEM/SERVICE` (#980 C1b; core §8.5, observer §7.5): a raw
observer across a constrained face subscribes by the scopes the contracts in
hand give for the address. That is each concrete resource's exact key and
each template's key with every parameter a wildcard, never `<ns>/zk2/**`,
under which every put would carry its key's text across the face. No
presence is read, since no descriptor crosses: keys resolve through
`--contracts` alone. `tests/live_zk2.rs`'s
`constrained_s7_a_tools_scope_across_a_face` runs the scope against a bus.

The cases here are its refusals, each made before a session opens, and each
this tool refusing what it was given: exit 2.

No descriptor crosses a face, so the scope comes from `--contracts`, and
without them there is none.

```console
$ zenctl echo --across-face host-a/tc
? 2
Error: --across-face builds its scope from the contracts in hand, since no descriptor crosses a face (observer §7.5): give --contracts

```

An address names one service. A wildcard there would subscribe wider than
what the tool reads.

```console
$ zenctl echo --across-face '*/tc' --contracts ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml
? 2
Error: --across-face */tc: system "*" is not a plain chunk ([a-z0-9]([a-z0-9._-]*[a-z0-9])?). Name one service, SYSTEM/SERVICE, each a plain chunk: a wildcard would subscribe wider than what this tool reads (core §8.5)

```

A selector typed beside it is narrowed to the face's scope, and one that
reaches none of it is refused.

```console
$ zenctl rate 'zk2/host-b/**' --across-face host-a/tc --contracts ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml
? 2
Error: zk2/host-b/** reaches none of the resources the contracts in hand give for host-a/tc across the face: type a selector under one of them, or none

```

A rule that reads presence or the doctor reads `@zk`, which does not cross a
face, so the watchdog refuses it there.

```console
$ zenctl watchdog --rule 'instance-gone host-a/tc' --across-face host-a/tc --contracts ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml
? 2
Error: watchdog --across-face: `instance-gone host-a/tc` reads presence or the doctor, which do not cross a constrained face (core §8.5): drop the rule, or ask it on the face's own side

```

A rule whose selector reaches none of the face's resources would watch
nothing there.

```console
$ zenctl watchdog --rule 'rate-below zk2/host-b/** 1' --across-face host-a/tc --contracts ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml
? 2
Error: watchdog --across-face: `rate-below zk2/host-b/** 1` watches zk2/host-b/**, which reaches none of the selectors across the face (zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/state/interfaces/*/* + zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/state/namespaces + zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/bandwidth/*/*)

```
